Strong Final Interview Answer

Streamlit is an open-source Python framework used to rapidly build interactive web applications and dashboards, especially for analytics, AI, and machine learning workloads. Streamlit simplifies frontend development by providing built-in widgets and visualization components without requiring HTML, CSS, or JavaScript. In Snowflake, Streamlit apps run natively inside the platform using Snowpark for data access and virtual warehouses for compute. Streamlit apps are schema-level objects managed by Snowflake security and access control, and they execute using owner’s rights, allowing users to access app outputs without direct table permissions.
